Do not allocate the MTP drafter's embed_tokens and lm_head: vLLM throws them away.

vLLM ALWAYS replaces an MTP drafter's own embed_tokens and lm_head with the
target model's after loading, on both model runners:

  * Model Runner V1: the proposer, v1/spec_decode/llm_base_proposer.py,
    _maybe_share_embeddings and _maybe_share_lm_head (their "MTP model"
    branch: an MTP drafter declares no has_own_embed_tokens / has_own_lm_head,
    so it always shares);
  * Model Runner V2, the default since 0.29 (vllm#53183): the MTP speculator
    loads its drafter with load_eagle_model in
    v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/eagle/utils.py, which shares whenever the drafter
    declares no copy of its own (_should_share); Qwen3.5's drafter declares none.

Until that moment both copies are resident. Qwen3.5/3.6/3.8 have a
248,320-row vocabulary, so that is 2 x 2.37 GiB (bf16) allocated, loaded from the
checkpoint, and then freed. Upstream still allocates both (0.30.0
qwen3_5_mtp.py:85 and :246).

On a 24 GiB card the second allocation does not fit next to a ~18 GiB model:
  torch.OutOfMemoryError: Tried to allocate 2.37 GiB ... 1.85 GiB is free
Measured identically on vLLM 0.22.1 and 0.28.0 with Qwen3.8-27B-MTP-NVFP4
(2026-09-19 / 2026-09-21), and on 2026-07-02 with Qwen3.6-27B-MTP-pi-tune-NVFP4.
It fails at MODEL LOAD, before any KV cache exists, so no serving flag
(--gpu-memory-utilization, --max-model-len, --enforce-eager) can reach it.

With this patch the drafter builds placeholders (PPMissingLayer) instead, skips
those tensors in load_weights, and the runner's sharing step fills them in as
before: V1 deletes the placeholder and assigns the target's layer; V2's
_should_share returns true for a drafter without has_own_* flags, and it then
does the same. Verified 2026-09-21 on RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell (vLLM 0.28.0,
Model Runner V1 path): "Model loading took 18.65 GiB" (17.86 GiB body + the MTP
layer), both "Sharing target model ..." lines logged, 40/40 requests served,
61.6 tok/s against 33.3 tok/s without MTP, mean acceptance length 2.6-3.4 at 3
draft tokens. Not yet run on 0.30.0 (V2 logs no sharing line).

Sharing only happens at pipeline-parallel size 1; the stock behaviour is kept
otherwise. DEVAI_MTP_SHARE_VOCAB_AT_INIT=0 restores it unconditionally.

Applies AFTER the HyperQwen series (qwen3_5-embed-quant and
qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab touch the same file), with `patch -p1 --fuzz 0`, on
both build records: vLLM 0.28.0 + HyperQwen c0c81bb and vLLM 0.30.0 + HyperQwen
7af097b (dry-run checked on both trees, 2026-10-07). The hunks are cut against
0.30.0; on 0.28.0 they apply at offsets with exact context.

